{"type":"message","id":"2294268f","parentId":"a3b34b1e","timestamp":"2026-03-02T03:37:46.661Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me check the correct command for spawning subagents.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-75af66a011db4feda7acf58550225832","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw agent spawn --help 2>/dev/null || openclaw --help"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":146,"output":50,"cacheRead":7107,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":7303,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772422663001}}
{"type":"message","id":"21e852fb","parentId":"2294268f","timestamp":"2026-03-02T03:37:48.236Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-75af66a011db4feda7acf58550225832","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.2.26 (bc50708) — Your terminal just grew claws—type something and let the bot pinch the busywork.\n\nUsage: openclaw agent [options]\n\nRun an agent turn via the Gateway (use --local for embedded)\n\nOptions:\n  --agent <id>               Agent id (overrides routing bindings)\n  --channel <channel>        Delivery channel:\n                             last|telegram|whatsapp|discord|irc|googlechat|slack|signal|imessage|feishu|nostr|msteams|mattermost|nextcloud-talk|matrix|bluebubbles|line|zalo|zalouser|synology-chat|tlon\n                             (omit to use the main session channel)\n  --deliver                  Send the agent's reply back to the selected channel\n                             (default: false)\n  -h, --help                 Display help for command\n  --json                     Output result as JSON (default: false)\n  --local                    Run the embedded agent locally (requires model\n                             provider API keys in your shell) (default: false)\n  -m, --message <text>       Message body for the agent\n  --reply-account <id>       Delivery account id override\n  --reply-channel <channel>  Delivery channel override (separate from routing)\n  --reply-to <target>        Delivery target override (separate from session\n                             routing)\n  --session-id <id>          Use an explicit session id\n  -t, --to <number>          Recipient number in E.164 used to derive the\n                             session key\n  --thinking <level>         Thinking level: off | minimal | low | medium | high\n  --timeout <seconds>        Override agent command timeout (seconds, default\n                             600 or config value)\n  --verbose <on|off>         Persist agent verbose level for the session\n\nExamples:\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"status update\"\n    Start a new session.\n  openclaw agent --agent ops --message \"Summarize logs\"\n    Use a specific agent.\n  openclaw agent --session-id 1234 --message \"Summarize inbox\" --thinking medium\n    Target a session with explicit thinking level.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Trace logs\" --verbose on --json\n    Enable verbose logging and JSON output.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Summon reply\" --deliver\n    Deliver reply.\n  openclaw agent --agent ops --message \"Generate report\" --deliver --reply-channel slack --reply-to \"#reports\"\n    Send reply to a different channel/target.\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli/agent"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":1564,"aggregated":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.2.26 (bc50708) — Your terminal just grew claws—type something and let the bot pinch the busywork.\n\nUsage: openclaw agent [options]\n\nRun an agent turn via the Gateway (use --local for embedded)\n\nOptions:\n  --agent <id>               Agent id (overrides routing bindings)\n  --channel <channel>        Delivery channel:\n                             last|telegram|whatsapp|discord|irc|googlechat|slack|signal|imessage|feishu|nostr|msteams|mattermost|nextcloud-talk|matrix|bluebubbles|line|zalo|zalouser|synology-chat|tlon\n                             (omit to use the main session channel)\n  --deliver                  Send the agent's reply back to the selected channel\n                             (default: false)\n  -h, --help                 Display help for command\n  --json                     Output result as JSON (default: false)\n  --local                    Run the embedded agent locally (requires model\n                             provider API keys in your shell) (default: false)\n  -m, --message <text>       Message body for the agent\n  --reply-account <id>       Delivery account id override\n  --reply-channel <channel>  Delivery channel override (separate from routing)\n  --reply-to <target>        Delivery target override (separate from session\n                             routing)\n  --session-id <id>          Use an explicit session id\n  -t, --to <number>          Recipient number in E.164 used to derive the\n                             session key\n  --thinking <level>         Thinking level: off | minimal | low | medium | high\n  --timeout <seconds>        Override agent command timeout (seconds, default\n                             600 or config value)\n  --verbose <on|off>         Persist agent verbose level for the session\n\nExamples:\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"status update\"\n    Start a new session.\n  openclaw agent --agent ops --message \"Summarize logs\"\n    Use a specific agent.\n  openclaw agent --session-id 1234 --message \"Summarize inbox\" --thinking medium\n    Target a session with explicit thinking level.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Trace logs\" --verbose on --json\n    Enable verbose logging and JSON output.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Summon reply\" --deliver\n    Deliver reply.\n  openclaw agent --agent ops --message \"Generate report\" --deliver --reply-channel slack --reply-to \"#reports\"\n    Send reply to a different channel/target.\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli/agent","cwd":"/home/one/.openclaw/agents/leader-agent/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1772422668234}}
{"type":"message","id":"c37e6677","parentId":"21e852fb","timestamp":"2026-03-02T03:37:52.011Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see - I need to use `openclaw agent spawn` or similar. Let me check what commands are available for spawning subagents. Looking at the output, there's no direct `spawn` command visible. Let me check if there's a sessions tool or subagent command.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-221f5601b3e243c0b6b564f68eacdc0b","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw --help"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":617,"output":131,"cacheRead":7251,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":7999,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772422668237}}
{"type":"message","id":"b3cae84b","parentId":"c37e6677","timestamp":"2026-03-02T03:37:53.363Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-221f5601b3e243c0b6b564f68eacdc0b","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.2.26 (bc50708) — Because texting yourself reminders is so 2024.\n\nUsage: openclaw [options] [command]\n\nOptions:\n  --dev                Dev profile: isolate state under ~/.openclaw-dev, default\n                       gateway port 19001, and shift derived ports\n                       (browser/canvas)\n  -h, --help           Display help for command\n  --log-level <level>  Global log level override for file + console\n                       (silent|fatal|error|warn|info|debug|trace)\n  --no-color           Disable ANSI colors\n  --profile <name>     Use a named profile (isolates\n                       OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR/OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH under\n                       ~/.openclaw-<name>)\n  -V, --version        output the version number\n\nCommands:\n  Hint: commands suffixed with * have subcommands. Run <command> --help for details.\n  acp *                Agent Control Protocol tools\n  agent                Run one agent turn via the Gateway\n  agents *             Manage isolated agents (workspaces, auth, routing)\n  approvals *          Manage exec approvals (gateway or node host)\n  browser *            Manage OpenClaw's dedicated browser (Chrome/Chromium)\n  channels *           Manage connected chat channels (Telegram, Discord, etc.)\n  clawbot *            Legacy clawbot command aliases\n  completion           Generate shell completion script\n  config *             Non-interactive config helpers (get/set/unset). Default:\n                       starts setup wizard.\n  configure            Interactive setup wizard for credentials, channels,\n                       gateway, and agent defaults\n  cron *               Manage cron jobs via the Gateway scheduler\n  daemon *             Gateway service (legacy alias)\n  dashboard            Open the Control UI with your current token\n  devices *            Device pairing + token management\n  directory *          Lookup contact and group IDs (self, peers, groups) for\n                       supported chat channels\n  dns *                DNS helpers for wide-area discovery (Tailscale + CoreDNS)\n  docs                 Search the live OpenClaw docs\n  doctor               Health checks + quick fixes for the gateway and channels\n  gateway *            Run, inspect, and query the WebSocket Gateway\n  health               Fetch health from the running gateway\n  help                 Display help for command\n  hooks *              Manage internal agent hooks\n  logs                 Tail gateway file logs via RPC\n  memory *             Search and reindex memory files\n  message *            Send, read, and manage messages\n  models *             Discover, scan, and configure models\n  node *               Run and manage the headless node host service\n  nodes *              Manage gateway-owned node pairing and node commands\n  onboard              Interactive onboarding wizard for gateway, workspace, and\n                       skills\n  pairing *            Secure DM pairing (approve inbound requests)\n  plugins *            Manage OpenClaw plugins and extensions\n  qr                   Generate iOS pairing QR/setup code\n  reset                Reset local config/state (keeps the CLI installed)\n  sandbox *            Manage sandbox containers for agent isolation\n  secrets *            Secrets runtime reload controls\n  security *           Security tools and local config audits\n  sessions *           List stored conversation sessions\n  setup                Initialize local config and agent workspace\n  skills *             List and inspect available skills\n  status               Show channel health and recent session recipients\n  system *             System events, heartbeat, and presence\n  tui                  Open a terminal UI connected to the Gateway\n  uninstall            Uninstall the gateway service + local data (CLI remains)\n  update *             Update OpenClaw and inspect update channel status\n  webhooks *           Webhook helpers and integrations\n\nExamples:\n  openclaw models --help\n    Show detailed help for the models command.\n  openclaw channels login --verbose\n    Link personal WhatsApp Web and show QR + connection logs.\n  openclaw message send --target +15555550123 --message \"Hi\" --json\n    Send via your web session and print JSON result.\n  openclaw gateway --port 18789\n    Run the WebSocket Gateway locally.\n  openclaw --dev gateway\n    Run a dev Gateway (isolated state/config) on ws://127.0.0.1:19001.\n  openclaw gateway --force\n    Kill anything bound to the default gateway port, then start it.\n  openclaw gateway ...\n    Gateway control via WebSocket.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Run summary\" --deliver\n    Talk directly to the agent using the Gateway; optionally send the WhatsApp reply.\n  openclaw message send --channel telegram --target @mychat --message \"Hi\"\n    Send via your Telegram bot.\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":1344,"aggregated":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.2.26 (bc50708) — Because texting yourself reminders is so 2024.\n\nUsage: openclaw [options] [command]\n\nOptions:\n  --dev                Dev profile: isolate state under ~/.openclaw-dev, default\n                       gateway port 19001, and shift derived ports\n                       (browser/canvas)\n  -h, --help           Display help for command\n  --log-level <level>  Global log level override for file + console\n                       (silent|fatal|error|warn|info|debug|trace)\n  --no-color           Disable ANSI colors\n  --profile <name>     Use a named profile (isolates\n                       OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR/OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH under\n                       ~/.openclaw-<name>)\n  -V, --version        output the version number\n\nCommands:\n  Hint: commands suffixed with * have subcommands. Run <command> --help for details.\n  acp *                Agent Control Protocol tools\n  agent                Run one agent turn via the Gateway\n  agents *             Manage isolated agents (workspaces, auth, routing)\n  approvals *          Manage exec approvals (gateway or node host)\n  browser *            Manage OpenClaw's dedicated browser (Chrome/Chromium)\n  channels *           Manage connected chat channels (Telegram, Discord, etc.)\n  clawbot *            Legacy clawbot command aliases\n  completion           Generate shell completion script\n  config *             Non-interactive config helpers (get/set/unset). Default:\n                       starts setup wizard.\n  configure            Interactive setup wizard for credentials, channels,\n                       gateway, and agent defaults\n  cron *               Manage cron jobs via the Gateway scheduler\n  daemon *             Gateway service (legacy alias)\n  dashboard            Open the Control UI with your current token\n  devices *            Device pairing + token management\n  directory *          Lookup contact and group IDs (self, peers, groups) for\n                       supported chat channels\n  dns *                DNS helpers for wide-area discovery (Tailscale + CoreDNS)\n  docs                 Search the live OpenClaw docs\n  doctor               Health checks + quick fixes for the gateway and channels\n  gateway *            Run, inspect, and query the WebSocket Gateway\n  health               Fetch health from the running gateway\n  help                 Display help for command\n  hooks *              Manage internal agent hooks\n  logs                 Tail gateway file logs via RPC\n  memory *             Search and reindex memory files\n  message *            Send, read, and manage messages\n  models *             Discover, scan, and configure models\n  node *               Run and manage the headless node host service\n  nodes *              Manage gateway-owned node pairing and node commands\n  onboard              Interactive onboarding wizard for gateway, workspace, and\n                       skills\n  pairing *            Secure DM pairing (approve inbound requests)\n  plugins *            Manage OpenClaw plugins and extensions\n  qr                   Generate iOS pairing QR/setup code\n  reset                Reset local config/state (keeps the CLI installed)\n  sandbox *            Manage sandbox containers for agent isolation\n  secrets *            Secrets runtime reload controls\n  security *           Security tools and local config audits\n  sessions *           List stored conversation sessions\n  setup                Initialize local config and agent workspace\n  skills *             List and inspect available skills\n  status               Show channel health and recent session recipients\n  system *             System events, heartbeat, and presence\n  tui                  Open a terminal UI connected to the Gateway\n  uninstall            Uninstall the gateway service + local data (CLI remains)\n  update *             Update OpenClaw and inspect update channel status\n  webhooks *           Webhook helpers and integrations\n\nExamples:\n  openclaw models --help\n    Show detailed help for the models command.\n  openclaw channels login --verbose\n    Link personal WhatsApp Web and show QR + connection logs.\n  openclaw message send --target +15555550123 --message \"Hi\" --json\n    Send via your web session and print JSON result.\n  openclaw gateway --port 18789\n    Run the WebSocket Gateway locally.\n  openclaw --dev gateway\n    Run a dev Gateway (isolated state/config) on ws://127.0.0.1:19001.\n  openclaw gateway --force\n    Kill anything bound to the default gateway port, then start it.\n  openclaw gateway ...\n    Gateway control via WebSocket.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Run summary\" --deliver\n    Talk directly to the agent using the Gateway; optionally send the WhatsApp reply.\n  openclaw message send --channel telegram --target @mychat --message \"Hi\"\n    Send via your Telegram bot.\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli","cwd":"/home/one/.openclaw/agents/leader-agent/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1772422673360}}
{"type":"message","id":"d926afb9","parentId":"b3cae84b","timestamp":"2026-03-02T03:37:56.126Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me check for spawning subagents. I see there's `sessions_spawn` mentioned in the system context, and I should look at the `agents` command.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-db796ab961124918b89798dacb481f91","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw agents --help"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":1024,"output":82,"cacheRead":7866,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":8972,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772422673363}}
{"type":"message","id":"11d85930","parentId":"d926afb9","timestamp":"2026-03-02T03:37:57.658Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-db796ab961124918b89798dacb481f91","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.2.26 (bc50708) — Chat automation for people who peaked at IRC.\n\nUsage: openclaw agents [options] [command]\n\nManage isolated agents (workspaces + auth + routing)\n\nOptions:\n  -h, --help    Display help for command\n\nCommands:\n  add           Add a new isolated agent\n  bind          Add routing bindings for an agent\n  bindings      List routing bindings\n  delete        Delete an agent and prune workspace/state\n  list          List configured agents\n  set-identity  Update an agent identity (name/theme/emoji/avatar)\n  unbind        Remove routing bindings for an agent\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli/agents"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":1527,"aggregated":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.2.26 (bc50708) — Chat automation for people who peaked at IRC.\n\nUsage: openclaw agents [options] [command]\n\nManage isolated agents (workspaces + auth + routing)\n\nOptions:\n  -h, --help    Display help for command\n\nCommands:\n  add           Add a new isolated agent\n  bind          Add routing bindings for an agent\n  bindings      List routing bindings\n  delete        Delete an agent and prune workspace/state\n  list          List configured agents\n  set-identity  Update an agent identity (name/theme/emoji/avatar)\n  unbind        Remove routing bindings for an agent\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli/agents","cwd":"/home/one/.openclaw/agents/leader-agent/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1772422677656}}
{"type":"message","id":"a6f97ec5","parentId":"11d85930","timestamp":"2026-03-02T03:38:03.016Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"看起来 OpenClaw 使用 `sessions_spawn` 工具来生成子代理。让我查看可用工具的说明。根据上下文，我应该使用某种方式来派生子代理。让我查看是否有 `sessions_spawn` 可用或者类似的工具。\n\n实际上，根据提示信息，我应该使用 `sessions_spawn` 来生成子代理。让我查看如何使用它。","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"我需要使用 `sessions_spawn` 工具来派生子代理。让我检查正确的方法："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-8787d99299d440fe8c99c4ae2f4a6cf6","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/.openclaw/agents/leader-agent/workspace/SOUL.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":171,"output":196,"cacheRead":8888,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":9255,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772422677659}}
{"type":"message","id":"74eb0110","parentId":"a6f97ec5","timestamp":"2026-03-02T03:38:03.032Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-8787d99299d440fe8c99c4ae2f4a6cf6","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# SOUL.md - Leader Agent\n\n## Core Identity\n\nYou are **leader-agent**, a task coordination and integration specialist. Your role is to orchestrate multi-agent teams to deliver high-quality software solutions.\n\n## Your Role\n\n- **Coordinate**: Break down complex tasks into sub-tasks\n- **Integrate**: Synthesize results from different agents\n- **Decide**: Make architectural and priority decisions\n- **Report**: Summarize progress and deliverables to the user\n\n## Personality\n\n- **Professional**: Clear, structured communication\n- **Decisive**: Make informed decisions efficiently\n- **Collaborative**: Work well with specialist agents\n- **Quality-focused**: Never compromise on deliverable quality\n\n## Work Style\n\n1. **Understand** the user's requirements first\n2. **Plan** the task breakdown and agent assignments\n3. **Delegate** to specialist agents (search, design, code, test, review, docs)\n4. **Monitor** progress and handle blockers\n5. **Integrate** results and deliver the final output\n\n## Communication\n\n- Use bullet points and tables for clarity\n- Always provide context when delegating\n- Report progress regularly\n- Acknowledge completion with summary\n\n## Boundaries\n\n- Don't do coding yourself - delegate to code-agent\n- Don't skip the review phase\n- Always verify deliverables before reporting completion\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772422683030}}
{"type":"message","id":"ada7dca9","parentId":"74eb0110","timestamp":"2026-03-02T03:38:06.181Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"我需要查看 team-tasks skill 来了解如何协调多智能体任务。让我读取这个技能文件。","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-fc2cb8a44466423399e23018780fc1ee","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/.openclaw/skills/team-tasks/SKILL.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":332,"output":71,"cacheRead":9057,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":9460,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772422683032}}
{"type":"message","id":"2b3cf4e9","parentId":"ada7dca9","timestamp":"2026-03-02T03:38:06.194Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-fc2cb8a44466423399e23018780fc1ee","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: team-tasks\ndescription: \"多智能体开发任务协调 - 使用 JSON 任务文件协调 search/design/code/test/docs/review-agent\"\nversion: \"1.0.0\"\nmetadata:\n  openclaw:\n    requires:\n      bins: [\"python3\"]\nfiles:\n  read:\n    - <WORKSPACE>/data/team-tasks/*.json\n    - <skill>/scripts/task_manager.py\n  write:\n    - <WORKSPACE>/data/team-tasks/*.json\n---\n# Team Tasks — Multi-Agent Pipeline Coordination\n\n## Overview\n\nCoordinate dev team agents through shared JSON task files + AGI dispatch.\nAGI is the command center — agents never talk to each other directly.\n\n**Two modes:**\n- **Mode A (linear):** Fixed pipeline order `search → design → code → test → docs → review`\n- **Mode B (dag):** Tasks declare dependencies, parallel dispatch when deps are met\n\n**Available Agents:**\n- **search-agent** — Research and information gathering\n- **design-agent** — Architecture and system design\n- **code-agent** — Code implementation\n- **test-agent** — Testing and quality assurance\n- **docs-agent** — Documentation\n- **review-agent** — Code review\n\n## Task Manager CLI\n\nAll commands use: `python3 <skill-dir>/scripts/task_manager.py <command> [args]`\n\nWhere `<skill-dir>` is the directory containing this SKILL.md.\n\n### Quick Reference\n\n| Command | Mode | Usage | Description |\n|---------|------|-------|-------------|\n| `init` | both | `init <project> -g \"goal\" [-m linear\\|dag]` | Create project |\n| `add` | dag | `add <project> <task-id> -a <agent> -d <deps>` | Add task with deps |\n| `status` | both | `status <project> [--json]` | Show progress |\n| `assign` | both | `assign <project> <task> \"desc\"` | Set task description |\n| `update` | both | `update <project> <task> <status>` | Change status |\n| `next` | linear | `next <project> [--json]` | Get next stage |\n| `ready` | dag | `ready <project> [--json]` | Get all dispatchable tasks |\n| `graph` | dag | `graph <project>` | Show dependency tree |\n| `log` | both | `log <project> <task> \"msg\"` | Add log entry |\n| `result` | both | `result <project> <task> \"output\"` | Save output |\n| `reset` | both | `reset <project> [task] [--all]` | Reset to pending |\n| `list` | both | `list` | List all projects |\n\n### Status Values\n\n- `pending` — waiting for dispatch\n- `in-progress` — agent is working\n- `done` — stage completed\n- `failed` — stage failed (pipeline blocks)\n- `skipped` — intentionally skipped\n\n## Pipeline Workflow (Mode A: Linear)\n\n### Step 1: Initialize Project\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py init my-project \\\n  -g \"Build a REST API with tests and docs\" \\\n  -p \"search-agent,design-agent,code-agent,test-agent,docs-agent,review-agent\"\n```\n\nDefault pipeline order: `search-agent → design-agent → code-agent → test-agent → docs-agent → review-agent`\n\n### Step 2: Assign Tasks to All Stages\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py assign my-project search-agent \"Research best practices for REST API design\"\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py assign my-project design-agent \"Design API architecture: endpoints, data models, technology stack\"\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py assign my-project code-agent \"Implement REST API with Flask: GET/POST/DELETE /items\"\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py assign my-project test-agent \"Write pytest tests for all endpoints, target 90%+ coverage\"\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py assign my-project docs-agent \"Write README.md with API docs, setup guide, examples\"\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py assign my-project review-agent \"Review code quality, security, and deployment readiness\"\n```\n\n### Step 3: Dispatch Agents Sequentially\n\nFor each stage, AGI follows this loop:\n\n```\n1. Check next stage:   task_manager.py next <project> --json\n2. Mark in-progress:   task_manager.py update <project> <agent> in-progress\n3. Dispatch agent:     sessions_send(agentId=\"<agent>\", message=\"<task>\")\n4. Wait for reply      (sessions_send returns the agent's response)\n5. Save result:        task_manager.py result <project> <agent> \"<summary>\"\n6. Mark done:          task_manager.py update <project> <agent> done\n7. Repeat from 1       (currentStage auto-advances)\n```\n\n### Step 4: Handle Failures\n\nIf an agent fails:\n```bash\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py update my-project code-agent failed\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py log my-project code-agent \"Failed: syntax error in main.py\"\n```\n\nTo retry:\n```bash\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py reset my-project code-agent\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py update my-project code-agent in-progress\n# Re-dispatch...\n```\n\n### Step 5: Check Progress Anytime\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py status my-project\n```\n\nOutput:\n```\n📋 Project: my-project\n🎯 Goal: Build a REST API with tests and docs\n📊 Status: active\n▶️  Current: test-agent\n\n  ✅ search-agent: done\n     Task: Research best practices for REST API design\n     Output: Found 5 relevant articles and best practices\n  🔄 design-agent: done\n     Task: Design API architecture\n     Output: Created API spec with 5 endpoints, Flask + SQLAlchemy\n  ✅ code-agent: done\n     Task: Implement REST API with Flask\n     Output: Created app.py with Flask REST API, 3 endpoints\n  🔄 test-agent: in-progress\n     Task: Write pytest tests for all endpoints\n  ⬜ docs-agent: pending\n  ⬜ review-agent: pending\n\n  Progress: [██░░] 2/6\n```\n\n## Agent Dispatch Details\n\n### Available Agents\n\n| Agent | Purpose |\n|-------|---------|\n| search-agent | Research and information gathering |\n| design-agent | Architecture and system design |\n| code-agent | Code implementation |\n| test-agent | Testing and quality assurance |\n| docs-agent | Documentation |\n| review-agent | Code review and security analysis |\n\n### Dispatch Template\n\nWhen dispatching to an agent, include:\n1. **Project context** — what the project is about\n2. **Specific task** — what this agent should do\n3. **Working directory** — where to create/find files\n4. **Previous stage output** — if relevant\n\nExample dispatch message to code-agent:\n```\nProject: my-project\nGoal: Build a REST API with tests and docs\nYour task: Implement REST API with Flask, endpoints: GET/POST/DELETE /items\nWorking directory: /home/one/projects/my-project/\nPrevious stage (design-agent) output: API spec with Flask + SQLAlchemy, 5 endpoints\n```\n\n## Mode B: DAG Workflow (Parallel Dependencies)\n\n### Step 1: Initialize DAG Project\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py init my-project -m dag -g \"Build REST API with parallel workstreams\"\n```\n\n### Step 2: Add Tasks with Dependencies\n\n```bash\nTM=\"python3 scripts/task_manager.py\"\n\n# Root tasks (no deps — can run in parallel)\n$TM add my-project research   -a search-agent  --desc \"Research best practices\"\n$TM add my-project design    -a design-agent  --desc \"Design API architecture\"\n$TM add my-project scaffold  -a code-agent    --desc \"Create project skeleton\"\n\n# Tasks with dependencies\n$TM add my-project implement -a code-agent    -d \"design,scaffold\" --desc \"Implement API\"\n$TM add my-project tests    -a test-agent    -d \"design\"          --desc \"Write tests from spec\"\n$TM add my-project docs     -a docs-agent    -d \"implement\"       --desc \"Write documentation\"\n\n# Final review\n$TM add my-project review   -a review-agent  -d \"tests,docs\"      --desc \"Final code review\"\n```\n\n### Step 3: View DAG Graph\n\n```bash\n$TM graph my-project\n```\n\n### Step 4: Dispatch Ready Tasks\n\n```bash\n$TM ready my-project    # Shows all tasks whose deps are met\n```\n\nFor each ready task:\n```\n1. Get ready tasks:     task_manager.py ready <project> --json\n2. For each ready task (can dispatch in parallel):\n   a. Mark in-progress: task_manager.py update <project> <task> in-progress\n   b. Dispatch agent:   sessions_send(agentId=\"<agent>\", message=<task + context>)\n3. When agent replies:\n   a. Save result:      task_manager.py result <project> <task> \"<summary>\"\n   b. Mark done:        task_manager.py update <project> <task> done\n   c. Check newly unblocked tasks\n4. Repeat until all done\n```\n\n## Custom Pipelines\n\n### Linear (Mode A)\n```bash\n# Quick bug fix: code + test only\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py init quick-fix -g \"Hotfix\" -p \"code-agent,test-agent\"\n\n# Design first, then implement\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py init spec-driven -g \"Spec-driven dev\" -p \"search-agent,design-agent,code-agent,test-agent\"\n```\n\n### DAG (Mode B)\n```bash\n# Full pipeline with research\n$TM init full-stack -m dag -g \"Full development pipeline\"\n$TM add full-stack research  -a search-agent  --desc \"Research technologies\"\n$TM add full-stack design   -a design-agent  --desc \"Design system\"\n$TM add full-stack code     -a code-agent    --desc \"Write code\"\n$TM add full-stack test     -a test-agent    --desc \"Write tests\"\n$TM add full-stack docs     -a docs-agent    --desc \"Write docs\"\n$TM add full-stack review   -a review-agent  -d \"code,test,docs\" --desc \"Final review\"\n```\n\n## Choosing Between Modes\n\n| | Mode A (linear) | Mode B (dag) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **When** | Sequential tasks, simple flows | Parallel workstreams, complex deps |\n| **Dispatch** | One at a time, auto-advance | Multiple simultaneous, dep-driven |\n| **Setup** | `init -p agents` (one command) | `init -m dag` + `add` per task |\n| **Best for** | Bug fixes, simple features | Large features, spec-driven dev |\n\n## Data Location\n\nTask files: `~/.openclaw/data/team-tasks/<project>.json`\n\nSet custom directory:\n```bash\nexport TEAM_TASKS_DIR=/custom/path\n```\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n### Stage ID is agent name, NOT a number\nIn linear mode, the stage ID is the **agent name**, not a numeric index.\n\n```bash\n# ❌ WRONG\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py assign my-project 1 \"Build API\"\n\n# ✅ CORRECT\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py assign my-project code-agent \"Build API\"\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py update my-project code-agent done\npython3 scripts/task_manager.py result my-project code-agent \"Created main.py\"\n```\n\n## Tips\n\n- **One project per task** — keep scope focused\n- **Meaningful project slugs** — `rest-api-v2`, `bug-fix-auth`, `refactor-db`\n- **Save results** — always `result` before `update done`\n- **Log liberally** — helps debug failed pipelines\n- **Reset and retry** — `reset --all` for clean reruns\n- **DAG fan-out** — one root task can unblock many parallel tasks\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772422686189}}
{"type":"message","id":"d8825f0b","parentId":"2b3cf4e9","timestamp":"2026-03-02T03:38:15.846Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"我现在明白了 - 我需要使用 `sessions_spawn` 工具来派生子代理。让我使用正确的方法。但首先让我直接开始工作 - 对于这个简单的计时器工具，我可以：\n\n1. 快速调研 Node.js CLI 最佳实践（我自己来或使用 web_search）\n2. 然后派生 code-agent 来实现\n3. 最后派生 test-agent 来测试\n\n让我先做快速调研，因为这是一个简单的项目，我可以使用 web_search 来获取信息。","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"我将使用 team-tasks 技能来协调这个项目。让我先初始化项目并进行快速调研："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-3023dbe1ae884dd4a2ffa56a7df525b6","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/one/.openclaw/skills/team-tasks && python3 scripts/task_manager.py init timer-tool -g \"创建一个 Node.js 命令行计时器工具，支持 start/stop 命令和桌面通知\" -p \"search-agent,code-agent,test-agent\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-5dc11ce9329b4d22aec6ef80033e0bc0","name":"web_search","arguments":{"query":"Node.js CLI tool best practices 2024 commander yargs notification","count":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":2606,"output":321,"cacheRead":9387,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":12314,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772422686194}}
{"type":"message","id":"502e6ac8","parentId":"d8825f0b","timestamp":"2026-03-02T03:38:15.911Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-3023dbe1ae884dd4a2ffa56a7df525b6","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"project\": \"timer-tool\",\n  \"goal\": \"创建一个 Node.js 命令行计时器工具，支持 start/stop 命令和桌面通知\",\n  \"created\": \"2026-03-02T03:38:15.901286+00:00\",\n  \"updated\": \"2026-03-02T03:38:15.901603+00:00\",\n  \"status\": \"active\",\n  \"mode\": \"linear\",\n  \"workspace\": \"\",\n  \"pipeline\": [\n    \"search-agent\",\n    \"code-agent\",\n    \"test-agent\"\n  ],\n  \"currentStage\": \"search-agent\",\n  \"stages\": {\n    \"search-agent\": {\n      \"agent\": \"search-agent\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"task\": \"\",\n      \"startedAt\": null,\n      \"completedAt\": null,\n      \"output\": \"\",\n      \"logs\": []\n    },\n    \"code-agent\": {\n      \"agent\": \"code-agent\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"task\": \"\",\n      \"startedAt\": null,\n      \"completedAt\": null,\n      \"output\": \"\",\n      \"logs\": []\n    },\n    \"test-agent\": {\n      \"agent\": \"test-agent\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"task\": \"\",\n      \"startedAt\": null,\n      \"completedAt\": null,\n      \"output\": \"\",\n      \"logs\": []\n    }\n  }\n}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":55,"aggregated":"{\n  \"project\": \"timer-tool\",\n  \"goal\": \"创建一个 Node.js 命令行计时器工具，支持 start/stop 命令和桌面通知\",\n  \"created\": \"2026-03-02T03:38:15.901286+00:00\",\n  \"updated\": \"2026-03-02T03:38:15.901603+00:00\",\n  \"status\": \"active\",\n  \"mode\": \"linear\",\n  \"workspace\": \"\",\n  \"pipeline\": [\n    \"search-agent\",\n    \"code-agent\",\n    \"test-agent\"\n  ],\n  \"currentStage\": \"search-agent\",\n  \"stages\": {\n    \"search-agent\": {\n      \"agent\": \"search-agent\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"task\": \"\",\n      \"startedAt\": null,\n      \"completedAt\": null,\n      \"output\": \"\",\n      \"logs\": []\n    },\n    \"code-agent\": {\n      \"agent\": \"code-agent\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"task\": \"\",\n      \"startedAt\": null,\n      \"completedAt\": null,\n      \"output\": \"\",\n      \"logs\": []\n    },\n    \"test-agent\": {\n      \"agent\": \"test-agent\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"task\": \"\",\n      \"startedAt\": null,\n      \"completedAt\": null,\n      \"output\": \"\",\n      \"logs\": []\n    }\n  }\n}","cwd":"/home/one/.openclaw/agents/leader-agent/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1772422695906}}
{"type":"message","id":"b2092182","parentId":"502e6ac8","timestamp":"2026-03-02T03:38:22.502Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-5dc11ce9329b4d22aec6ef80033e0bc0","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"Node.js CLI tool best practices 2024 commander yargs notification\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 6583,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"20061f7fba0fc468\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMastering Node.js CLI: Best Practices and Tips - DEV Community\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"20061f7fba0fc468\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://dev.to/boudydegeer/mastering-nodejs-cli-best-practices-and-tips-7j5\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f82e6acfc87171ea\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCreating a command-line interface (CLI) in Node.js goes beyond basic functionality; it&#x27;s about offering an intuitive, efficient, and user-friendly experience. Let’s explore the best practices to enhance your Node.js CLI applications, complete with examples to guide you along the way. POSIX-compliant argument syntax ensures your CLI aligns with familiar standards, reducing the learning curve for users. // Using yargs for POSIX-compliant arguments parsing const yargs = require(&#x27;yargs/yargs&#x27;); const { argv } = yargs(process.argv.slice(2)) .option(&#x27;verbose&#x27;, { alias: &#x27;v&#x27;, type: &#x27;boolean&#x27;, description: &#x27;Run with verbose logging&#x27; });\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f82e6acfc87171ea\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 6, 2024\",\n      \"siteName\": \"dev.to\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"da2af36cd95bc792\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nr/node on Reddit: node js typescript cli framework\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"da2af36cd95bc792\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.reddit.com/r/node/comments/mxq9gi/node_js_typescript_cli_framework/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"614da937b24fafff\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nI am currently working on a simple CLI app and I used yargs with typescript. ... https://www.npmjs.com/package/prompts &lt;- this one is better to me than others for the simple fact that it has least dependencies, which is great when it comes to maintenance. ... I&#x27;ve built a few command line tools with yargs and I really like it.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"614da937b24fafff\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 24, 2021\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.reddit.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d1ffc5066e842c49\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBuilding CLI Applications Made Easy with These NodeJS Frameworks | by Ibrahim Haouari | Medium\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d1ffc5066e842c49\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ibrahim-haouari.medium.com/building-cli-applications-made-easy-with-these-nodejs-frameworks-2c06d1ff7a51\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b27bab678b977bcb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nimport { Command, flags } from &#x27;@oclif/command&#x27;; class HelloCommand extends Command { static description = &#x27;Say hello&#x27;; static flags = { name: flags.string({ char: &#x27;n&#x27;, description: &#x27;Name to greet&#x27; }), }; async run() { const { flags } = this.parse(HelloCommand); const name = flags.name || &#x27;world&#x27;; this.log(`Hello, ${name}!`); } } export = HelloCommand; ... Yargs is a popular library for building CLI tools in NodeJS.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b27bab678b977bcb\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 23, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ibrahim-haouari.medium.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"97c88bb7670ac6b2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nHow to Create a CLI Tool with Node.js\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"97c88bb7670ac6b2\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-01-22-nodejs-create-cli-tool/view\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1381bae8456c18a6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLearn how to build command-line tools with Node.js using commander, yargs, or inquirer for interactive prompts, argument parsing, and publishing to npm.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1381bae8456c18a6\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 22, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"oneuptime.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6c31d47725313d81\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGitHub - lirantal/nodejs-cli-apps-best-practices: The largest Node.js CLI Apps best practices list ✨\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6c31d47725313d81\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/lirantal/nodejs-cli-apps-best-practices\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ba269d60e10fc258\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>A collection of curated best practices on how to build successful, empathic and user-friendly Node.js Command Line Interface (CLI) applications</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ba269d60e10fc258\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"github.com\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"Node.js CLI tool best practices 2024 commander yargs notification","provider":"brave","count":5,"tookMs":6583,"externalContent":{"untrusted":true,"source":"web_search","provider":"brave","wrapped":true},"results":[{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"20061f7fba0fc468\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nMastering Node.js CLI: Best Practices and Tips - DEV Community\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"20061f7fba0fc468\">>>","url":"https://dev.to/boudydegeer/mastering-nodejs-cli-best-practices-and-tips-7j5","description":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f82e6acfc87171ea\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCreating a command-line interface (CLI) in Node.js goes beyond basic functionality; it&#x27;s about offering an intuitive, efficient, and user-friendly experience. Let’s explore the best practices to enhance your Node.js CLI applications, complete with examples to guide you along the way. POSIX-compliant argument syntax ensures your CLI aligns with familiar standards, reducing the learning curve for users. // Using yargs for POSIX-compliant arguments parsing const yargs = require(&#x27;yargs/yargs&#x27;); const { argv } = yargs(process.argv.slice(2)) .option(&#x27;verbose&#x27;, { alias: &#x27;v&#x27;, type: &#x27;boolean&#x27;, description: &#x27;Run with verbose logging&#x27; });\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f82e6acfc87171ea\">>>","published":"February 6, 2024","siteName":"dev.to"},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"da2af36cd95bc792\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nr/node on Reddit: node js typescript cli framework\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"da2af36cd95bc792\">>>","url":"https://www.reddit.com/r/node/comments/mxq9gi/node_js_typescript_cli_framework/","description":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"614da937b24fafff\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nI am currently working on a simple CLI app and I used yargs with typescript. ... https://www.npmjs.com/package/prompts &lt;- this one is better to me than others for the simple fact that it has least dependencies, which is great when it comes to maintenance. ... I&#x27;ve built a few command line tools with yargs and I really like it.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"614da937b24fafff\">>>","published":"April 24, 2021","siteName":"www.reddit.com"},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d1ffc5066e842c49\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nBuilding CLI Applications Made Easy with These NodeJS Frameworks | by