{"type":"message","id":"ad60ecbd","parentId":"2c3b7e60","timestamp":"2026-03-02T03:39:41.791Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The write tool is restricted to the workspace. Let me create the files in the workspace and then copy them to the target location, or use a different approach. Since I can use exec to write files, let me use that.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"我需要在工作区创建文件，然后复制到目标位置："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-eadfa6e268ec447b8a7be964537db51b","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/.openclaw/agents/leader-agent/workspace/timer-tool/package.json","content":"{\n  \"name\": \"timer-cli\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"description\": \"A simple command-line timer tool with desktop notifications\",\n  \"main\": \"index.js\",\n  \"bin\": {\n    \"timer\": \"./index.js\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"test\": \"node test.js\"\n  },\n  \"keywords\": [\"timer\", \"cli\", \"countdown\"],\n  \"author\": \"\",\n  \"license\": \"MIT\",\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"commander\": \"^12.0.0\"\n  }\n}"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-ae93addf8dcc48b2944fca64c9b5272c","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/.openclaw/agents/leader-agent/workspace/timer-tool/index.js","content":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n\nconst { Command } = require('commander');\nconst { spawn } = require('child_process');\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst path = require('path');\n\nconst program = new Command();\nconst PID_FILE = path.join(require('os').tmpdir(), 'timer-cli.pid');\nconst LOG_FILE = path.join(require('os').tmpdir(), 'timer-cli.log');\n\n// Format seconds to MM:SS\nfunction formatTime(seconds) {\n  const mins = Math.floor(seconds / 60);\n  const secs = seconds % 60;\n  return `${mins.toString().padStart(2, '0')}:${secs.toString().padStart(2, '0')}`;\n}\n\n// Send desktop notification (cross-platform)\nfunction sendNotification(title, message) {\n  const platform = process.platform;\n  \n  if (platform === 'darwin') {\n    // macOS\n    spawn('osascript', ['-e', `display notification \"${message}\" with title \"${title}\"`]);\n  } else if (platform === 'linux') {\n    // Linux - try notify-send\n    spawn('notify-send', [title, message]);\n  } else if (platform === 'win32') {\n    // Windows - use PowerShell\n    spawn('powershell', [\n      '-Command',\n      `[System.Reflection.Assembly]::LoadWithPartialName(\"System.Windows.Forms\") | Out-Null; [System.Windows.Forms.MessageBox]::Show(\"${message}\", \"${title}\")`\n    ]);\n  }\n}\n\n// Start the timer\nfunction startTimer(seconds) {\n  // Check if timer is already running\n  if (fs.existsSync(PID_FILE)) {\n    const pid = parseInt(fs.readFileSync(PID_FILE, 'utf8').trim());\n    try {\n      process.kill(pid, 0); // Check if process exists\n      console.error('Timer is already running. Use \"timer stop\" to stop it first.');\n      process.exit(1);\n    } catch (e) {\n      // Process doesn't exist, clean up\n      fs.unlinkSync(PID_FILE);\n    }\n  }\n\n  console.log(`Timer started: ${formatTime(seconds)}`);\n  \n  // Fork a background process for the timer\n  const child = spawn(process.execPath, [__filename, '--run-timer', seconds.toString()], {\n    detached: true,\n    stdio: 'ignore'\n  });\n  \n  // Save PID\n  fs.writeFileSync(PID_FILE, child.pid.toString());\n  \n  child.unref();\n  console.log(`Timer running in background (PID: ${child.pid})`);\n  console.log('You will be notified when the timer completes.');\n}\n\n// Run timer countdown (internal command)\nfunction runTimer(seconds) {\n  let remaining = seconds;\n  \n  const interval = setInterval(() => {\n    remaining--;\n    \n    if (remaining <= 0) {\n      clearInterval(interval);\n      sendNotification('⏰ Timer Complete!', `Timer finished after ${formatTime(seconds)}`);\n      \n      // Clean up PID file\n      if (fs.existsSync(PID_FILE)) {\n        fs.unlinkSync(PID_FILE);\n      }\n      process.exit(0);\n    }\n    \n    // Write remaining time to log file for status checks\n    fs.writeFileSync(LOG_FILE, `${remaining}`);\n  }, 1000);\n}\n\n// Stop the timer\nfunction stopTimer() {\n  if (!fs.existsSync(PID_FILE)) {\n    console.log('No timer is running.');\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const pid = parseInt(fs.readFileSync(PID_FILE, 'utf8').trim());\n  \n  try {\n    process.kill(pid, 'SIGTERM');\n    console.log(`Timer stopped (PID: ${pid})`);\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.log('Timer was not running (process not found).');\n  }\n  \n  // Clean up\n  if (fs.existsSync(PID_FILE)) {\n    fs.unlinkSync(PID_FILE);\n  }\n  if (fs.existsSync(LOG_FILE)) {\n    fs.unlinkSync(LOG_FILE);\n  }\n}\n\n// Show timer status\nfunction showStatus() {\n  if (!fs.existsSync(PID_FILE)) {\n    console.log('No timer is running.');\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const pid = parseInt(fs.readFileSync(PID_FILE, 'utf8').trim());\n  \n  try {\n    process.kill(pid, 0);\n    \n    let remaining = 'unknown';\n    if (fs.existsSync(LOG_FILE)) {\n      remaining = formatTime(parseInt(fs.readFileSync(LOG_FILE, 'utf8').trim()));\n    }\n    \n    console.log(`Timer running (PID: ${pid})`);\n    console.log(`Time remaining: ${remaining}`);\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.log('No timer is running (stale PID file).');\n    fs.unlinkSync(PID_FILE);\n  }\n}\n\n// Parse command line arguments\nprogram\n  .name('timer')\n  .description('A simple command-line timer with notifications')\n  .version('1.0.0');\n\nprogram\n  .command('start <seconds>')\n  .description('Start a countdown timer')\n  .action((seconds) => {\n    const secs = parseInt(seconds);\n    if (isNaN(secs) || secs <= 0) {\n      console.error('Please provide a valid number of seconds (> 0)');\n      process.exit(1);\n    }\n    startTimer(secs);\n  });\n\nprogram\n  .command('stop')\n  .description('Stop the running timer')\n  .action(() => {\n    stopTimer();\n  });\n\nprogram\n  .command('status')\n  .description('Show timer status')\n  .action(() => {\n    showStatus();\n  });\n\n// Hidden internal command for background timer\nprogram\n  .option('--run-timer <seconds>', 'Internal: run timer in background', (val, prev) => {\n    runTimer(parseInt(val));\n    process.exit(0);\n  });\n\nprogram.parse();"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-952a1f83b635408380868b8af406a501","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/.openclaw/agents/leader-agent/workspace/timer-tool/test.js","content":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n\nconst { execSync, spawn } = require('child_process');\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst path = require('path');\nconst os = require('os');\n\nconst PID_FILE = path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'timer-cli.pid');\nconst LOG_FILE = path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'timer-cli.log');\nconst TIMER_SCRIPT = path.join(__dirname, 'index.js');\n\nconsole.log('🧪 Timer CLI Tests\\n');\n\n// Clean up any existing timer state\nfunction cleanup() {\n  if (fs.existsSync(PID_FILE)) fs.unlinkSync(PID_FILE);\n  if (fs.existsSync(LOG_FILE)) fs.unlinkSync(LOG_FILE);\n}\n\n// Test helper\nfunction test(name, fn) {\n  try {\n    fn();\n    console.log(`✅ ${name}`);\n    return true;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.log(`❌ ${name}`);\n    console.log(`   Error: ${error.message}`);\n    return false;\n  }\n}\n\n// Run tests\ncleanup();\n\nlet passed = 0;\nlet total = 5;\n\n// Test 1: Help command works\npassed += test('Help command displays usage', () => {\n  const output = execSync(`node ${TIMER_SCRIPT} --help`).toString();\n  if (!output.includes('timer') || !output.includes('start')) {\n    throw new Error('Help output missing expected content');\n  }\n});\n\n// Test 2: Start command requires seconds argument\npassed += test('Start command validates input', () => {\n  try {\n    execSync(`node ${TIMER_SCRIPT} start invalid`, { stdio: 'pipe' });\n    throw new Error('Should have failed with invalid input');\n  } catch (e) {\n    if (!e.stderr) throw e; // Expected to fail\n  }\n});\n\n// Test 3: Timer starts and creates PID file\npassed += test('Timer start creates PID file', () => {\n  // Start a 10 second timer\n  execSync(`node ${TIMER_SCRIPT} start 10`);\n  \n  // Check PID file exists\n  if (!fs.existsSync(PID_FILE)) {\n    throw new Error('PID file not created');\n  }\n  \n  // Verify PID is a number\n  const pid = parseInt(fs.readFileSync(PID_FILE, 'utf8').trim());\n  if (isNaN(pid)) {\n    throw new Error('PID file contains invalid data');\n  }\n});\n\n// Test 4: Stop command removes PID file\npassed += test('Timer stop removes PID file', () => {\n  execSync(`node ${TIMER_SCRIPT} stop`);\n  \n  // Wait a moment for cleanup\n  const start = Date.now();\n  while (fs.existsSync(PID_FILE) && Date.now() - start < 1000) {\n    // Wait for cleanup\n  }\n  \n  if (fs.existsSync(PID_FILE)) {\n    throw new Error('PID file not removed after stop');\n  }\n});\n\n// Test 5: Status shows no timer when stopped\npassed += test('Status shows no timer when stopped', () => {\n  const output = execSync(`node ${TIMER_SCRIPT} status`).toString();\n  if (!output.includes('No timer is running')) {\n    throw new Error('Status should indicate no timer running');\n  }\n});\n\nconsole.log(`\\n📊 Results: ${passed}/${total} tests passed`);\n\n// Final cleanup\ncleanup();\n\nprocess.exit(passed === total ? 0 : 1);"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-5c1229d732d54bf4a27f3620fcc12c27","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/.openclaw/agents/leader-agent/workspace/timer-tool/README.md","content":"# Timer CLI\n\nA simple command-line timer tool with desktop notifications.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\ncd timer-tool\nnpm install\nnpm link  # Makes 'timer' command available globally\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Start a timer\n```bash\ntimer start <seconds>\n```\n\nExamples:\n```bash\ntimer start 60     # 1 minute timer\ntimer start 300    # 5 minute timer\ntimer start 1500   # 25 minute (Pomodoro) timer\n```\n\n### Stop the timer\n```bash\ntimer stop\n```\n\n### Check timer status\n```bash\ntimer status\n```\n\n## Features\n\n- **Background operation**: Timer runs in the background, you can close the terminal\n- **Desktop notifications**: Get notified when the timer completes (works on macOS, Linux, and Windows)\n- **PID tracking**: Prevents multiple timers from running simultaneously\n- **Status check**: See remaining time with `timer status`\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Node.js 14 or higher\n- For notifications on Linux: `notify-send` (usually available via `libnotify-bin`)\n\n## Technical Details\n\n- Uses `commander` for CLI argument parsing (following Node.js CLI best practices)\n- Spawns a detached child process for background timer\n- Uses OS temp directory for PID/LOG files\n- Cross-platform notification support\n\n## Development\n\n```bash\n# Run tests\nnpm test\n\n# Run without linking\nnode index.js start 10\n```\n\n## License\n\nMIT"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":333,"output":2564,"cacheRead":14297,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":17194,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772422721822}}
